Subject: [PATCH] LM Studio as a local text provider for summaries, documents and chat

LM Studio becomes its own text provider beside Ollama: no API key, its server address filled in
with LM Studio's default (http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1), counted as local (allowed in local-only mode,
no cost). OpenPlod never starts LM Studio; when its server is off, settings and requests say how to
turn it on. Settings list LM Studio's chat models (embedding models left out) with their context
sizes, offer Test connection and one button to use LM Studio for summaries, documents and chat.
A request larger than the context LM Studio loaded the model with is refused before sending, and
checked again after the answer (a model loaded on demand may get a smaller context): an answer built
from a cut transcript is never saved and never falls back to a cloud provider. A reasoning model's
<think> block is removed from answers. AI Chat and Create document describe local providers as
running on this computer. Document batches accept every text provider.
